# Coach speech (Polish): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang (its header documents every placeholder).
#
# Always positive, never blaming. The coach says "ty" and is male ("wygrałem", "musiałem"); the
# player's gender is unknown: no second-person past tense or conditional ("wygrałeś", "znalazłeś"),
# no adjective about the player ("gotowy"). Instead: "udało ci się", "szło ci", impersonal forms
# ("można było zbić"), nouns ("wygrana była w twoich rękach", "pozycja była wygrana"), the present
# tense, or "we" ("zremisowaliśmy", "cofnęliśmy": virile, right for a mixed pair).
# Move numbers are ordinals (common.lang): "w {n:nth_move_loc}" = "w 21. ruchu" (spoken "w
# dwudziestym pierwszym ruchu"), "{n:nth_move}" = "21. ruch", "do {crit_no:nth_move_gen}" = "do 21.
# ruchu". A move ({move}, {crit_best} ...) is spoken as its piece in the nominative ("skoczek ef
# trzy", "krótka roszada" is feminine), so no case and no past-tense agreement hangs on it: the noun
# "ruch" carries them ("ruch {crit_best} był lepszy", "zamiast ruchu {crit_move}"), or the line uses
# the present tense ("{move} wygrywa materiał"), "a nie" / "niż" (nominative) or no verb.
# Counts that can be zero (mistakes, checks, captures) stay in the nominative ("0 błędów").
# Accuracy: "{acc:percent}" = "85%" (spoken "osiemdziesiąt pięć procent"), only where a nominative
# or accusative fits (after a colon, "wyniosła", "miałem", "kontra"), never after "z dokładnością".
# {eval} is always a pawn evaluation here ("+1,3", "równowaga"): "mniej więcej {eval}" (not "około",
# which needs the genitive).
# Names inserted by {text}, {theme}, {level}:
#   appraisal.phase.*   nominatives "debiut" (m), "gra środkowa" (f), "końcówka" (f); their cases
#                       ("{text:loc}" = "w debiucie") are in common.lang; no verb or adjective agrees
#                       with {text} ("{text} to twoja najlepsza faza").
#   appraisal.reason.*  a complement right after "Remis" ("Remis przez pata.", "zakończyła się
#                       remisem za zgodą"), no comma before it.
#   theme.*             a verbal-noun phrase in the nominative, lower case, no full stop ("patrzenie
#                       na całą szachownicę przed ruchem"), always after a colon, so it never takes a
#                       case; "swój" for the player's own pieces.
#   appraisal.level.*   the level names of the coach page (coach.level.N.name), said inside „…” after
#                       "poziom": "na poziom „Początkujący”", "spróbuj poziomu „Ekspert”".
# {opening:def} is the opening's name as used inside a sentence (lower-case nominative, from the
# opening texts), always after a colon or "to"; "{opening}" alone as a whole line.

# ---- Names used inside the lines ------------------------------------------------------------------
